# Revert Guide: Luna Band `Noise_REP_XXXX` Bluetooth Name Change

## Purpose
- This document explains exactly how to revert the Bluetooth-name support change that:
  - allowed `Noise_REP_XXXX` scan results to enter the existing Luna-band pipeline
  - displayed renamed devices as `Noise Band` in UI
  - kept legacy devices displayed as `Luna Band`
- Use this only if you want to fully remove this rename-support change set and return to the older behavior where only the legacy Luna-band BLE naming is recognized by the app.

## Scope of the change set
- No backend API contract was changed.
- No Gradle/build/dependency file was changed.
- No SDK/AAR integration file was changed.
- No database/storage schema was changed.
- No existing pairing/connection flow branching by `deviceType` was changed.
- The production code change is intentionally limited to the existing scan-classification ViewModel and its UI-facing display label.

## Files affected by this change set

| File | Mode in this change set | What changed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `app/src/main/java/com/noisefit/ui/onboarding/pairing/find/SearchNearbyDeviceViewModel.kt` | Modified | Added `Noise_REP_` fallback matching and separate UI display-name resolution |
| `app/src/test/java/com/noisefit/ui/onboarding/pairing/find/SearchNearbyDeviceViewModelTest.kt` | Created | Added focused regression tests for old/new name handling |
