  - `31-33`
- Added code:
  - `LUNA_BAND_NOISE_REP_PREFIX`
  - `LUNA_BAND_DISPLAY_NAME`
  - `NOISE_BAND_DISPLAY_NAME`
- Revert action:
  - delete lines `31-33`

### 1.2 Remove extracted helper for catalog name matching
- Current lines:
  - `35-48`
- Added code:
  - `internal fun ColorFitNetworkDevice.matchesScannedDeviceName(scannedName: String): Boolean`
- Purpose of added code:
  - moved the pre-existing inline matcher logic out of `getDeviceType(...)`
- Revert action:
  - delete lines `35-48`
  - restore the original inline matching logic inside `getDeviceType(...)`

### 1.3 Remove `Noise_REP_` alias resolver
- Current lines:
  - `50-63`
- Added code:
  - `internal fun resolveLunaBandNoiseRepAlias(...)`
- Purpose of added code:
  - maps scanned names beginning with `Noise_REP_` to the existing `DeviceType.LUNA_BAND` catalog entry only as a fallback
- Revert action:
  - delete lines `50-63`

### 1.4 Remove UI display-name resolver
- Current lines:
  - `65-74`
- Added code:
  - `internal fun resolveScannedDeviceDisplayName(...)`
- Purpose of added code:
  - returns `Noise Band` for `Noise_REP_XXXX`
  - returns the matched catalog name for legacy Luna-band devices
- Revert action:
  - delete lines `65-74`

### 1.5 Revert the `ColorFitDevice.bluetoothName` assignment in `onDeviceFound(...)`
- Current lines:
  - `283-287`
- Current code behavior:
  - `ColorFitDevice.bluetoothName` is set from `resolveScannedDeviceDisplayName(...)`
- Revert action:
  - replace current assignment at lines `284-287` with the old direct catalog-name assignment:

```kotlin
bluetoothName = result.second.bluetoothName,
```

- Why this matters:
  - the nearby-device list and pairing screen both already read `ColorFitDevice.bluetoothName`
  - reverting this line removes the separate `Noise Band` / `Luna Band` UI label behavior

### 1.6 Revert `getDeviceType(...)` to the pre-change matcher-only behavior
- Current lines:
  - `404-417`
- Current code behavior:
  - reads `scannedName`
  - runs `device.matchesScannedDeviceName(scannedName)`
  - if no catalog match is found, falls back to `resolveLunaBandNoiseRepAlias(devices, scannedName)`
- Revert action:
  - replace the full current body of `getDeviceType(...)` with the original matcher-only version below:

```kotlin
fun getDeviceType(scannedDevice: DeviceEntity): Pair<DeviceType?, ColorFitNetworkDevice>? {
    _deviceList.value?.forEach { device ->
        if (device.namePattern.isNullOrEmpty() || device.matchingType.isNullOrEmpty()) return@forEach
        device.namePattern?.split(";")?.forEach {
            when (device.matchingType) {
                "exact" -> {
                    if (scannedDevice.name?.equals(it, true) == true) {
                        return Pair(
                            DeviceType.findDeviceType(device.deviceType!!),
                            device
                        )
                    }
                }

                "exact_pattern" -> {
                    if (scannedDevice.name?.dropLast(5)?.equals(it, true) == true) {
                        return Pair(
                            DeviceType.findDeviceType(device.deviceType!!),
                            device
                        )
                    }
                }

                "pattern" -> {
                    if (scannedDevice.name?.contains(it, true) == true) {
                        return Pair(
                            DeviceType.findDeviceType(device.deviceType!!),
                            device
                        )
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    return null
}
```

- Result after revert:
  - `Noise_REP_XXXX` devices will no longer be recognized
  - only the legacy catalog-driven Luna-band naming will pass scan classification

## Why the UI changed without touching other pairing screens
- No pairing/pipeline screen code was edited for the label split.
- The changed scan-model name flows through existing UI bindings:
  - `app/src/main/java/com/noisefit/ui/onboarding/pairing/pair/NearbyDevicesAdapter.kt`
    - current line `36` appends `colorFitDevice.bluetoothName`
  - `app/src/main/java/com/noisefit/ui/onboarding/pairing/pair/PairingFragment.kt`
    - current line `716` assigns `binding.tvWatchName.text = colorFitDevice.bluetoothName`
  - `app/src/main/java/com/noisefit/ui/onboarding/pairing/find/FindDeviceListFragment.kt`
    - current lines `572-577` pass the scanned `ColorFitDevice` list into the adapter
- Revert implication:
  - do not change these UI files when reverting this Bluetooth-name change set
  - reverting `SearchNearbyDeviceViewModel.kt` is sufficient to remove the separate `Noise Band` label behavior

