## Summary of exact add/remove intent
- Added in production code:
  - `Noise_REP_` prefix support
  - fallback mapping from renamed devices to `DeviceType.LUNA_BAND`
  - UI display label `Noise Band` for renamed devices
  - explicit display label constant `Luna Band` for legacy devices
- Not added:
  - no new backend behavior
  - no new BLE connect path
  - no new SDK call handling
  - no new dependency
  - no new folder/module/package
- Deleted by this change set:
  - nothing

## Safe revert order
1. Revert `SearchNearbyDeviceViewModel.kt` production code changes.
2. Delete `SearchNearbyDeviceViewModelTest.kt`.
3. Remove the top Bluetooth-name sections from `changes.md` and `changes_detailed.md`.
4. Delete `update_changes.md`.
5. Verify that `Noise_REP_XXXX` devices no longer appear as supported Luna-band scan results.
6. Delete `revert_bluetooth_namechnage.mds` last.

## Expected behavior after full revert
- `Noise_REP_XXXX` devices will not be matched into `DeviceType.LUNA_BAND`.
- Only the older Luna-band naming pattern will be recognized.
- Nearby scan list and pairing UI will stop showing `Noise Band` because `ColorFitDevice.bluetoothName` will again come directly from the matched catalog entry.
